<section class="bg-base-100">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-[90rem] gap-10 px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-center lg:gap-14">
    <img src="/media/washing-hands.jpg" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-box object-cover lg:col-span-5" width="1600" height="1200">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <p class="caps text-secondary">If you were wrapped in film</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.25rem,4.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[0.95]" data-rise>Three to five days, then off in the shower</h2>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/85">
        <li class="flex gap-4"><span class="gothic text-[1.75rem] leading-none text-secondary">1</span>Leave the clear adhesive film on for three to five days, even if ink pools under it.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-4"><span class="gothic text-[1.75rem] leading-none text-secondary">2</span>Take it off in a warm shower: find an edge and peel it back slowly, along the skin, not up and away.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-4"><span class="gothic text-[1.75rem] leading-none text-secondary">3</span>Wash with fragrance-free soap, pat dry with a paper towel, and start the thin layer of ointment.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
